## The source statement

[AbsTopIII], Corollary 1.10, (i) [text: papers/motizuki_corpus/text/
Topics in Absolute Anabelian Geometry III.txt, lines 2094-2146; the following
(d) is at lines 2167-2178]:

  (i) There exists a functorial 'group-theoretic' algorithm for reconstructing
      the natural isomorphism H^2(G_k, mu_hat^Z(G_k)) --> Z-hat [cf. (a)],
      together with the natural surjection
      H^1(G_k, mu_hat^Z(G_k)) --> G_k^ab -->> Z-hat [cf. (b)], from the
      profinite group G_k, as follows:
   (a) mu_{Q/Z}(G_k) := colim_H (H^ab)_tors,
       mu_hat^Z(G_k) := Hom(Q/Z, mu_{Q/Z}(G_k)), H ranging over the open
       subgroups of G_k, the arrows of the direct limit induced by the
       Verlagerung (transfer) map.  [Thus the underlying module is unaffected
       by passing from G_k to an open subgroup.]  Then one constructs
       H^2(G_k, mu_hat^Z(G_k)) --> Z-hat 'group-theoretically' from G_k.
   (b) By applying the isomorphism of (a) [and the cup product in group
       cohomology], one constructs the surjection
       H^1(G_k, mu_hat^Z(G_k)) --> G_k^ab -->> G_k^unr --> Z-hat
       determined by the Frobenius element in the maximal unramified quotient.
   (d) ... the image of the Kummer map k^times --> H^1(G_k, mu_hat^Z(Pi_X))
       is the inverse image of the subgroup generated by the Frobenius element
       via the surjection of (b).

So the source algorithm has three layers: (1) the group-theoretic cyclotome
mu_hat^Z(G_v) together with the H^2-normalization H^2(G_v, mu_hat^Z) = Z-hat;
(2) the resulting normalized surjection H^1(G_v, mu_hat^Z) -->> Z-hat; and
(3) the identification of the inverse image of the nonnegative part with the
Kummer image of the local field's integral monoid.  The present tree already
has the actual local-field side: S2000 constructs the actual coefficient
cyclotome Hom(Q/Z, mu), the actual limit lim_J H^1(J, mu_hat^Z) over the open
subgroups of G_v, and the actual Kummer map on O^tri_{Qbar_p}; S2006 proves
that Kummer map injective and identifies its image with the nonzero integral
monoid.  What is missing at the source level is the *group-theoretic*
reconstruction (1) + (2) and its comparison (3) with the actual cyclotome and
Kummer image.

## What this file proves (unconditional, no sorry, no axiom)

**The G_v-action on the actual cohomological limit.**
germAction p : G_v ->* MulAut (PsiCnsCohomology p).  For g in
G_v = Gal(Qbar_p/Q_p) and a germ represented by a continuous cocycle c on an
open subgroup U, the translate is the cocycle

    x |--> g . c(g^{-1} x g)      on  g U g^{-1},

which is again a continuous crossed homomorphism and whose germ depends only on
the germ of c (translateRep_equivalent).  This proves:

* translateGerm_one, translateGerm_mul: the translate is a monoid homomorphism
  of the limit;
* translateGerm_conj, translateGerm_conj', translateGermEquiv: it is a
  multiplicative equivalence with inverse the translate by g^{-1};
* germAction, germAction_group_mul, germAction_act_one, germAction_act_mul: the
  assignment is a genuine action of G_v by group automorphisms of
  lim_J H^1(J, mu_hat^Z).

This is exactly the action used in the source: the coefficient action
PsiCnsCoefficientAction p on values together with the conjugation action on the
open subgroups over which the limit is taken.

## The exact first missing, in dependency order (no fake interface)

(M1) **Transfer/Verlagerung and the colimit itself.**  mu_{Q/Z}(G_v) is
     *defined* as the direct limit of the torsion of the abelianizations of the
     open subgroups, along the transfer maps.  Mathlib has no Verlagerung map
     for a finite-index (here open) subgroup, and no colimit of that shape is
     formable, so the very first missing item is the construction of these
     transition maps.  Nothing in this file asserts or assumes them.

(M2) **Local reciprocity on torsion.**  At the level of one open subgroup
     U = Gal(Qbar_p / L), the source identification is (U^ab)_tors = mu(L)
     (roots of unity in the fixed field).  This is local class field theory on
     torsion; it is stated below as localReciprocityOnTorsion p and is *not*
     proved here.  Caveat recorded deliberately: Abelianization U is Mathlib's
     abstract abelianization, while the source's (U^ab) is the profinite
     (closed-commutator) abelianization; the two agree on torsion only under
     additional finite-generation input, so the statement below is the
     abstract-torsion avatar of the source identification, not a literal
     transcription.

(M3) **Continuous H^2 and H^2(G_v, mu_hat^Z) = Z-hat.**  The tree has no
     continuous H^2 at all (only Iut.Foundations.ContinuousH1), and Z-hat is
     not in the tree either.  Mathematically the source's computation is
     H^2(G_v, mu_hat^Z) = lim_n Br(k_v)[n] = lim_n Z/n = Z-hat, i.e. local
     class field theory's Br(k_v) = Q/Z together with the cyclotomic
     identification of mu_hat^Z.  Neither Br, its invariant map, nor Z-hat
     exists here, so this item currently cannot even be *stated*.  It is
     recorded here as a comment, and no Lean declaration is fabricated for it.

(M4) **The normalized surjection and the Kummer-image comparison.**  The
     strongest statement on the tree's carriers is weakFrobeniusNormalization p
     below: a surjective homomorphism from the actual limit to the Frobenius
     component whose kernel meets the actual Kummer image exactly in the unit
     image.  It is a *weakening* of the source's
     H^1(G_v, mu_hat^Z) -->> Z-hat in two respects, both forced by the tree:
     the target is Multiplicative Integer instead of Z-hat, and the domain is
     the whole limit instead of H^1(G_v, mu_hat^Z).  Passing from Integer back
     to Z-hat, and identifying H^1(G_v, mu_hat^Z) with G_v^ab (the
     Hilbert-90/Tate input used by the source in (b)), are further missing
     steps, recorded here and not assumed.

(M5) **Joint continuity of the action.**  The action is constructed, but the
     tree puts *no topology* on PsiCnsCohomology p, so joint continuity cannot
     be stated.  Research note (not formalised, and asserted nowhere):
     PsiCnsCohomology p is a quotient of the disjoint union of the discrete
     sets H^1(J, mu_hat^Z) over all open subgroups J; the final (colimit)
     topology of these discrete stages is the discrete topology, for which
     joint continuity is vacuous.  Hence the paper's statement must be about
     the pro-discrete ind-topology, which needs the finite groups
     H^1(J, mu_n) = L^times/(L^times)^n (local CFT again) on the stages.
     This is the same class of gap as S1973's
     PsiCnsJointContinuousActionMissing and S1975's IndCarrierBallNeighborhood.


(M6) **Model comparison caveat.**  The Kummer image used by S2000/S2006 is the
     image of O^tri_{Qbar_p} (the nonzero integral elements of the algebraic
     closure), whereas the source's (d) is about k_v^times inside the limit;
     the normalization (M4) is exactly what cuts the limit down to the
     local-field-sized piece.  Without (M3)/(M4) the two images cannot be
     compared on the tree's carriers.

(M7) **G_v-equivariance of the actual Kummer map.**  The action constructed
     here is not yet compared with the actual Kummer map: the statement
     PsiCnsKummer (g . a) = germAction p g (PsiCnsKummer a), for a in O^tri,
     is not proved in this file.  A concrete route (not carried out): transport
     the canonical compatible root system of a along g, observe that the ratio
     cocycle of the transported system is exactly the translate
     x |--> g . c(g^{-1} x g) of the ratio cocycle of a, and use the
     root-choice independence of the germ (IntegralKummerRootRealization.germ_eq)
     to conclude.  Until this is done, the action is the source's action on the
     coefficient module and on the open subgroups, but the Kummer-image
     comparison of (d) still needs (M3), (M4) as well.

